# SwiftFormat configuration for apps/ios.
#
# Phase 1 (lint/format/logging guardrails) of the iOS clean-code milestone.
# Default rule set only, aside from the two exceptions below — the milestone's
# hardest constraint is zero user-visible change, including layout, and a
# broad default autoformat pass (whitespace, ordering, literal formatting,
# pattern hoisting) is the intended first commit.

# Mirrors project.yml's targets.Rawkoon.settings.base.SWIFT_VERSION exactly.
# The two must be bumped together in the same commit in the Swift 6 phase, or
# SwiftFormat emits syntax the compiler does not yet accept at the old
# language version.
--swiftversion 5.0

# Deletes SwiftUI `Group` wrappers, which changes the view tree's static
# type — the thing SwiftUI uses for identity, diffing and transitions. A dry
# run on macbuild found 51 sites in this tree, and this milestone forbids any
# user-visible change including layout, so this rule stays off.
--disable redundantSwiftUIGroup

# Same class of risk: drops a result-builder attribute and changes the
# resulting view's static type. 2 sites in this tree.
--disable redundantViewBuilder
